  "implemented": [
    "Winning KF metadata preserves raw authored weight and ordered transform target/priority bytes, including duplicate names. Imported node blend thresholds/only-highest flags survive inactive controllers; ambiguous bindings are explicit.",
    "Original one/two/many-slot normalization, signed priority comparison, threshold distinctions and optional translation/quaternion/scale composition use native float stores. The two-slot threshold path intentionally retains its observed double write to the second weight.",
    "Animation.setNativeSequenceLayers projects caller-owned ordered track samples through actual NIF callbacks. It uses current/winning sources and raw per-node priorities, samples private track clones, updates equal-topology frame values without rebuilding, and rejects missing/ambiguous or malformed requests before replacing the plan.",
    "Sampling finishes before node channel publication. Callback copies have independent frames; zero-weight tracks are not sampled. Projection participates in animated physical-target sampling and releases on model/scene teardown."
  ],
